        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(channels): share plugin contract scaffolds",
        "body": "Closes #105759\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nChannel plugins separately maintained the same approval authorization, secret registry, config UI-hint, and allowlist-resolution scaffolds. The copies had already drifted, making fixes and contract changes easy to apply inconsistently.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds parameterized Plugin SDK helpers for the shared contracts, then migrates the matching channel implementations while preserving channel-owned normalization and wildcard semantics. Native approval rendering and probe implementations remain channel-local because their behavior is materially different.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Plugin maintainers get one tested implementation for repeated channel contract logic, with 1,272 duplicated lines removed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Fresh autoreview: clean after fixing the missing-sender wildcard authorization finding.\n- `pnpm test src/plugin-sdk/approval-auth-helpers.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/channel-config-ui-hints.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/channel-secret-basic-runtime.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/directory-runtime.test.ts extensions/slack/src/approval-auth.test.ts`: 14 tests passed.\n- `pnpm build`: passed; Plugin SDK declarations 5,081,640 / 5,100,000 bytes.\n- `pnpm check:changed`: passed on the pre-publish base, including API baseline, SDK exports/surface budgets, typechecks, lint, and cycle guards.\n- `pnpm test:extensions`: full sweep passed before the final moving-main rebase. Latest-base rerun passed all shards through Signal and the focused Slack authorization tests; the Testbox process was OOM-killed during the broad Slack shard after 35 minutes, with no test failure. Hosted CI supplies final exact-head proof.\n",
